The directed join of a nonempty directed family of approximable maps, acting elementwise by directed union of the images.

<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`iSupMap`).** The directed supremum of a nonempty directed family of approximable maps relates neighbourhoods when some member of the family does.

*Proof.* Master uses any index; intersection finds a common upper bound in the directed family; monotonicity is inherited from any witnessing member. ∎

**Theorem (`mem_toElementMap_iSupMap`).** Membership in the elementwise image of the directed supremum is membership in the image of some member of the family.

*Proof.* Reassociate the witnessing neighbourhood and index. ∎
